      "extract": "If the space--time is not a differentiable manifold but a non--commutative geometry there may be interesting new physical effects. Because of the non existence of sufficiently developed differential calculus on the non--commutative geometry to study physical effects one needs new mathematical tools. Since on the other hand the quantum group spaces are natural examples for the non--commutative geometries it is of",
